  "notes": [
    "These nine metrics are the reference scenario's vital signs, not the twelve balance metrics of contracts.md §7. Six of §7's twelve describe mechanics that have not shipped — raids, god actions, worship, prestige — and the rest need per-node and per-(species, tier) telemetry that the §4.1 observation does not carry, so no executor in this tree can produce them yet.",
    "The universe these numbers describe is still degenerate, and every item is an open finding rather than something this baseline settles: node discovery plateaus well short of the 51 v1 nodes; every scripted strategy produces the same universe because no system reads a god action; the population halves before it grows; and several observation channels saturate. Grimoire shelving is the one item that has been fixed since the first baseline.",
    "referencePeakPopulation still has a standard error of exactly zero and therefore a tolerance of exactly zero, so the gate demands exact equality of it. That is deliberate: a deterministic sweep cannot move by chance, so a metric that has never varied has no noise behind which a real change could hide. referenceLibraryDepth was such a metric until this regeneration, and the zero tolerance is what caught it moving.",
    "Sample size is 200 runs over 4 parameter cells at 60 world ticks, sized so the gate runs in about a minute on four workers and can therefore run on every push. The 10,000-run instrument is balance/sweeps/balance-full.sweep.json, which is not runnable on this build — balance/README.md has the arithmetic."
  ],
